From: rebased from vllm-project/vllm PR #37750
Subject: fix: specify device for torch.Event to prevent multi-GPU issues

Rebased from PR #37750 (closed unmerged 2026-03-25) onto v0.22.0 line numbers.
The pooling-path hunk uses `async_output_copy_stream.device` instead of
`raw_pooler_output.device` per gemini-code-assist's review comment on the PR
(PoolerOutput = Tensor | list[Tensor] | list[Tensor|None], so `.device`
attribute access is unsafe on the union; the stream's device is always present).

